#!/usr/bin/env bash
# PATH shim: refuse ydotool inside the agent desktop.
#
# ydotool writes to /dev/uinput, creating a kernel evdev device. That device is
# picked up by libinput and delivered to seat0 — Ben's real session. The nested
# compositor has no libinput backend at all (its device list is just
# wl_pointer/wl_keyboard proxied from the parent), so ydotool input can never
# reach the agent desktop. It only ever types into Ben's screen.
#
# Failing loudly here turns a silent wrong-session action into an error.

cat >&2 <<'EOF'
ydotool is blocked inside the agent desktop.

It injects at the kernel uinput layer, which routes to seat0 — Ben's real
session — never this nested compositor. Using it would type into his screen.

Use socket-scoped tools instead (they target WAYLAND_DISPLAY/the instance):
  wtype 'some text'
  wtype -k Return
  hyprctl dispatch movecursor <X> <Y>
  hyprctl dispatch sendshortcut ',mouse:272,activewindow'    # left click
  grim out.png                                               # or: agentdesk shot
EOF
exit 1
